WEBVTT

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:54.780
Mr. Jack.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.660
I wanted to meet you.

00:02:01.530 --> 00:02:03.740
Wait until I'm done eating.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:20.720
Did I rush you?

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:26.890
No, I rushed myself.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:35.360
It looked like there would be something
more magnificent than food.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.070
Well, I don't know about that.

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:42.530
It will be magnificent for me.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.540
But I wonder if it will be
magnificent to you.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.750
Shall we go out?

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.010
I wanted somewhere more spacious,

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:02.590
but we would stand out in the daytime.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:04.970
This is fine.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:11.310
I heard that you use steroids.

00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.560
Does that bother you?

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:15.860
No.

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:21.650
Taking steroids doesn't make something
instantly attainable.

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:25.870
You were runner-up
in the Maximum Tournament.

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.830
We have time,
so take some if you would like to.

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.830
I heard that rumor.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.840
Seems like you rearranged boxing
into a martial art.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:40.590
I can't wait.

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:54.100
I apologize if this question is personal.

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:58.980
Can we expect you to return to the ring?

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:03.490
You've received thousands of punches
in your long career.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:05.490
That's a given, but...

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:09.200
<i>it has seriously destroyed your body.</i>

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:15.460
Many experts say that
returning to how you were before

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.250
is already a lost cause.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:22.340
But I can't help but hope.

00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:24.380
You're a treasure to mankind...

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.350
Champ?

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:34.480
Thank you, Champ. That's enough.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.770
It was my mistake.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.610
You've already done enough...

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:46.240
Help...

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.130
Who could believe this?

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.960
The 60-year-old champion with an illness

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.130
can still move just like his golden days.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:10.850
If it's just for one minute,
I'm still the world champion.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.600
And...

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:17.730
boxing didn't destroy me.

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:20.360
My son...

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:24.570
My son destroyed me.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.870
<i>What kind of man is he?</i>

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.620
<i>Is Baki Hanma...</i>

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.210
<i>stronger than this monster?</i>

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.420
<i>He's so big.</i>

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.640
<i>He's so heavy.</i>

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:54.930
<i>And he's so tough.</i>

00:05:58.020 --> 00:05:59.400
<i>He's so fast.</i>

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:05.150
<i>So tenacious.</i>

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:12.830
<i>He's so powerful.</i>

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:15.160
<i>He's so strong.</i>

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:22.170
<i>And this man,</i>

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.920
<i>while harboring so much potential,</i>

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:31.590
<i>is thorough.</i>

00:06:38.520 --> 00:06:39.690
<i>And persistent.</i>

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.080
<i>And a perfectionist.</i>

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:30.740
When I get hit,

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.410
I stand back up.

00:07:51.340 --> 00:07:53.220
<i>I always stand back up.</i>

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:58.470
<i>And I fight.</i>

00:08:02.230 --> 00:08:03.350
<i>Always.</i>

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:05.310
<i>No matter what.</i>

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.440
<i>Always.</i>

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.160
<i>Stand and fight!</i>

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:50.690
Come at me...

00:08:52.030 --> 00:08:54.200
Come on...

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:58.950
Now's your chance.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.420
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:09:15.550 --> 00:09:17.840
<i>I can't help it if he runs.</i>

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.810
5 DAYS LATER

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.850
What happened?

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:27.440
Just some stuff.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.190
Are you okay?

00:09:33.230 --> 00:09:37.110
I wanted you to cheer me up.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:40.450
You're having trouble talking.

00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:48.620
I had surgery.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.300
Sorry if it's hard to understand me.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:56.380
Does it sting? Do you want something cold?

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:05.100
I can come and meet you like this
if you ask me to.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:09.730
But you shouldn't expect
anything more from me.

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:19.110
That's fine as long as you come see me.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:22.330
Sorry, young lady.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:25.910
Can I borrow this big guy?

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.410
Mr. Shibukawa.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:29.290
Come on, big guy.

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:33.920
I completely forgot.

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:36.260
I'm sorry, Kozue.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:40.430
I forgot I had something important
with Mr. Shibukawa.

00:10:51.190 --> 00:10:52.520
So many lies.

00:10:54.610 --> 00:10:58.110
There's a lot of greenery here
despite being a city area.

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:03.370
Lots of empty space too.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:05.950
It's perfect for playing around.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.500
Sorry for making you
play along back there.

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:11.040
I don't get it.

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:14.170
We already finished our fight.

00:11:18.340 --> 00:11:23.510
It wasn't a real fight,
and I thought I would be fine if I lost,

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:26.720
but I couldn't let it go.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:30.850
A loss is a loss,
even if it's all fun and games.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:32.230
A game?

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:37.230
Leaving it as a loss
didn't sit well with me.

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:41.490
That wasn't a real fight to you?

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:46.990
You wanted a real fight?

00:11:48.330 --> 00:11:49.790
I understand.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.500
Shall we have a real fight?

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:02.880
<i>That wasn't a real fight?</i>

00:12:04.430 --> 00:12:05.340
<i>That...</i>

00:12:06.600 --> 00:12:09.430
<i>That was an incredibly tense fight.</i>

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:14.770
<i>Even at that old age,</i>
<i>he's such a sore loser!</i>

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:21.860
Hey, big guy.

00:12:21.940 --> 00:12:23.070
This will hurt.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:38.170
We're having a real fight, big guy.

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.510
Stop spacing out, you fucking moron.

00:12:52.180 --> 00:12:53.060
Hey, big guy.

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:57.020
Looks like you're in trouble.

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:09.030
Let's see... Here!

00:13:10.620 --> 00:13:11.540
Here!

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.790
Here. Here. Here.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:17.000
Here.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:18.330
Here.

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:22.590
That was a good workout.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:25.550
What will you do, big guy?

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.090
Do you want to go at it a bit more?

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.600
Let's meet again, big guy.

00:13:39.150 --> 00:13:40.270
Sorry.

00:13:41.690 --> 00:13:44.400
I wanted to dress a bit more nicely.

00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:50.320
You fought Mr. Shibukawa, didn't you?

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:53.990
It wasn't a fight.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:56.210
Idiot.

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.500
-What?
-"Fight until you die."

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:04.000
"The strong one is me."
"No, I'm the strong one."

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:06.510
"No, I am."

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:09.890
Idiots from Planet Strong.

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:15.470
You're hurt because of me.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:18.020
What? Not at all.

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.060
Mr. Orochi?

00:14:24.650 --> 00:14:27.240
He's calling for
the idiot from Planet Strong.

00:14:29.860 --> 00:14:30.870
I'm sorry.

00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.290
It's fine.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:43.920
Here's a suitable lot.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:47.210
One or two people pass by
every five minutes.

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:51.300
We just need to end it
within three minutes.

00:14:53.010 --> 00:14:56.850
A few days ago, you fought me in
a fight to the death.

00:14:57.390 --> 00:14:59.310
And you lost.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.560
Didn't we decide the winner?

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:06.820
Yes, that fight was undoubtedly
your win, boy.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.610
But so what?

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:12.820
I'm here in front of you,
wanting to fight.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:15.830
So what will you do?

00:15:15.910 --> 00:15:20.750
It's normal to stand in front of someone
and ask for a fight in our world.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:25.590
But I'm not at my best right now.

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:31.800
What? You're not possibly thinking
that asking an injured person for a fight

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:35.600
is cowardly, are you?

00:15:36.930 --> 00:15:40.600
When humans live, they eat and drink.

00:15:41.390 --> 00:15:44.360
They get hurt and sick too.

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:47.610
You shouldn't hope for
your best condition.

00:15:48.030 --> 00:15:50.360
That's how our world works.

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:52.110
Right, boy?

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.450
I don't want to fight you again.

00:15:58.450 --> 00:16:00.700
Try and make me say that.

00:16:01.410 --> 00:16:04.420
Come on, make me never want to
fight you again.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.880
Okay, I accept.

00:16:11.220 --> 00:16:14.050
I'll make a box now.

00:16:18.220 --> 00:16:19.850
Fists are boxes.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:25.150
The boxes smash into each other
and compete, thus becoming boxing.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:28.650
There won't be a third time.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.110
This will be a knockout for you.

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.490
After which,
I'll stomp on your feet over and over

00:16:36.070 --> 00:16:37.320
with all my strength.

00:16:38.240 --> 00:16:40.120
And as you ask for forgiveness,

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:43.660
I'll never forgive you,
and I'll keep stomping.

00:16:44.250 --> 00:16:47.250
Even if you cry, beg, or pray.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:51.800
I'll never forgive you,
and I'll keep stomping.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.930
Are you done talking?

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.060
Then allow me to begin.

00:17:10.400 --> 00:17:12.190
Don't you know, boy?

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:15.070
<i>Using your forehead against fists</i>

00:17:15.150 --> 00:17:19.370
<i>was a basic defense</i>
<i>back in the time of bare-knuckle fighting.</i>

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:27.420
Oh, geez!
You're already breathing heavily.

00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:30.340
Are you okay without that box?

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.850
I will never forgive you.

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:52.270
What's with that face?

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:56.990
It's common sense to attack
your opponent's weakness in a fight.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:12.340
Geez, "come on"? Seriously?

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:16.510
You made me wait for you to make a glove.

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:21.260
Well, in any case, maybe this will be
somewhat more of a fight.

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:31.900
Oh, he's mad!

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:38.400
That's not a fist anymore.

00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:47.250
Okay, boy.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:50.920
Now you've lost all your weapons.

00:18:51.290 --> 00:18:53.380
I'll be leaving now.

00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:57.420
It's your choice
whether we keep going or not.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.760
You can attack me from behind if you want,

00:19:01.140 --> 00:19:03.930
or leave me alone if you accept defeat.

00:19:04.680 --> 00:19:06.390
You decide.

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:18.570
Hey.

00:19:19.030 --> 00:19:21.610
-You're...
-It's fine.

00:19:24.070 --> 00:19:26.030
You're more injured every time we meet.

00:19:28.040 --> 00:19:30.960
Yes, that's what's important.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:34.170
What's important?

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.920
I'm more injured every time we meet.

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:40.470
So what does that mean?

00:19:42.050 --> 00:19:45.350
It means we've met many times.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:50.230
You're right.
We meet because we're friends.

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:55.360
What we call our relationship
isn't important.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:58.230
We're taking baby steps,

00:19:58.690 --> 00:20:01.650
but we're starting to understand
each other.

00:20:03.110 --> 00:20:05.740
For example, you like lemon tea.

00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:07.990
And I like hot coffee.

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:09.950
That kind of thing...

00:20:10.250 --> 00:20:13.830
And we're in the process of making rules.

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:19.250
Your seat is near the entrance,
and I'm near the back.

00:20:20.920 --> 00:20:22.880
What happened with Director Orochi?

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.680
Doppo Orochi...

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:35.440
What an awful way to lose.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.400
-I haven't lost.
-What?

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:48.280
You're so uncool.

00:21:01.510 --> 00:21:02.380
<i>It doesn't...</i>

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.010
It doesn't seem manly.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.060
<i>"Doesn't seem manly"?</i>

00:21:16.140 --> 00:21:18.230
I apologize for disturbing your rest.

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:23.940
A guest would like to see you
in the sub-basement Peacock Room.

00:21:26.910 --> 00:21:28.070
Are you okay?

00:21:28.700 --> 00:21:29.830
Who is it?

00:21:30.530 --> 00:21:34.830
The guest wanted me
to keep their name a secret.

00:21:36.080 --> 00:21:39.840
<i>Isn't the Peacock Room</i>
<i>reserved for parties?</i>

00:21:40.670 --> 00:21:43.050
<i>I can't have a party in this condition.</i>

00:21:43.920 --> 00:21:47.090
The guest is waiting alone.

00:21:47.930 --> 00:21:48.840
Yes.

00:21:49.680 --> 00:21:50.720
Alone?

00:21:52.640 --> 00:21:53.930
We have arrived.

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:05.740
Dad? Why are you here?

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:08.530
To fight.

00:22:08.780 --> 00:22:11.330
You're having a fight?

00:22:12.120 --> 00:22:12.990
With who?

00:22:13.660 --> 00:22:15.870
With you, Junior.

00:22:17.290 --> 00:22:18.620
Without the gloves.

00:23:42.290 --> 00:23:43.210
IDIOTS FROM PLANET STRONG
